6. Thermal Viability Margin

6.1 Dynamics and Discretization Error

C^{\mathrm{th}} \dot{T} = Q^{\mathrm{in}}(a) - Q^{\mathrm{out}}(T), \qquad Q^{\mathrm{out}}(T) = h(T - T_{\mathrm{env}}) + \varepsilon_{\mathrm{rad}} \sigma(T^4 - T_{\mathrm{env}}^4).
\tag{6.1}

The explicit Euler scheme has local truncation error

|e_{\mathrm{disc}}| \le \frac{\Delta t^2}{2} \sup_{T \in [T_{\mathrm{env}}, T^{\max}]} |g'(T)\, g(T)|, \qquad g(T) = \frac{Q^{\mathrm{in}}(a) - Q^{\mathrm{out}}(T)}{C^{\mathrm{th}}}.
\tag{6.2}

The units are temperature. The error belongs to the discrete map  f , not to the continuous plant, so it is not double-counted.

6.2 Margin and Boundary Condition

Define the action-dependent margin

\mathcal{S}^\circ_T(a) = \bigl\{\hat{T} : \hat{T} \le T^\circ(a)\bigr\}, \qquad T^\circ(a) = T^{\max} - 2\varepsilon - \frac{\Delta t\, Q^{\mathrm{in}}(a)}{C^{\mathrm{th}}} - \Delta T_{\mathrm{disc}},
\tag{6.3}

with  \Delta T_{\mathrm{disc}} = \sup |e_{\mathrm{disc}}| . The boundary condition is evaluated at the true margin edge  T^\circ(a) + \varepsilon , not at  T^{\max} :

Q^{\mathrm{out}}\bigl(T^\circ(a) + \varepsilon\bigr) \ge Q^{\mathrm{in}}(a) + \frac{C^{\mathrm{th}}\, \Delta T_{\mathrm{disc}}}{\Delta t}.
\tag{6.4}

Proposition 6.1 (Invariance). Suppose  Q^{\mathrm{out}}  is non-decreasing on  [T_{\mathrm{env}}, T^{\max}]  and (6.4) holds. Then  \mathcal{S}^\circ_T(a)  is controlled-invariant under action  a .

Proof. Let  \hat{T} \le T^\circ(a) , so the true  T \le T^\circ(a) + \varepsilon . Then

T_{t+1} \le T^\circ(a) + \varepsilon + \frac{\Delta t}{C^{\mathrm{th}}}\bigl(Q^{\mathrm{in}}(a) - Q^{\mathrm{out}}(T^\circ(a) + \varepsilon)\bigr) + \Delta T_{\mathrm{disc}} \le T^\circ(a) + \varepsilon,
\tag{6.5}

where the last inequality uses (6.4). The next estimate satisfies  \hat{T}_{t+1} \le T_{t+1} + \varepsilon \le T^\circ(a) + 2\varepsilon . The margin (6.3) is defined with  2\varepsilon , so  \hat{T}_{t+1} \le T^\circ(a) .  \square 

Remark 6.2. v1.2 evaluated the cooling condition at  T^{\max} . One max-heating step from the margin edge leaves the margin by  \Delta t\,Q^{\mathrm{in}}/C^{\mathrm{th}}  unless cooling offsets it at the edge. The correct point is  T^\circ(a) + \varepsilon , which is strictly below  T^{\max}  by  \varepsilon + \Delta T_{\mathrm{disc}} .

6.3 Action-Dependent Non-Emptiness

 \mathcal{S}^\circ_T(a)  is non-empty whenever  T^\circ(a) > T_{\mathrm{env}} . The action-independent margin is

\mathcal{S}^\circ_T = \bigcup_{a \in \hat{\mathcal{A}}(\hat{x})} \mathcal{S}^\circ_T(a),
\tag{6.6}

which is the set of temperatures from which some admissible action keeps the node cool. For the zero-compute action with  Q^{\mathrm{in}} = Q^{\mathrm{aux}} , the non-emptiness condition is

T^{\max} > T_{\mathrm{env}} + 2\varepsilon + \frac{\Delta t\, Q^{\mathrm{aux}}}{C^{\mathrm{th}}} + \Delta T_{\mathrm{disc}}.
\tag{6.7}

