11.4 The  p_{\mathrm{eff}}  Caveat

Substituting  p_{\mathrm{eff}} = \pi_{\mathrm{nom}} p_0 + \pi_{\mathrm{deg}} p_1  into the independent formula is conservative only for  r = 1 . For  r > 1 , it underestimates failure under common cause, because all replicas fail simultaneously. The two-state transient model (11.5)–(11.6) is the correct treatment.

