12. Architecture and LLM as Heuristic Designer

The validator is the sole component inside the trust boundary; it is deterministic, total, and sound with respect to the model. The estimator, baseline, optimizer, and LLM are outside and can only propose actions. Fallback is the deterministic constrained optimizer, which itself passes through the validator; if rejected, the system enters the safe state, and the event is logged as a feasibility failure distinct from a constraint violation.

The LLM is reframed as a heuristic designer: it proposes candidate heuristics or parameter settings for the constrained optimizer, not direct schedules. The optimizer evaluates them, and the validator filters the resulting actions.

Hypothesis 12.1. The LLM-assisted heuristic outperforms the fixed-priority baseline by at least  X\%  on metric  Y  for instances of size  Z , at a latency cost of at most  W  ms. The experiment measures  X, Y, Z, W  and reports whether the hypothesis is supported. No theoretical guarantee and no safety authority attach to the LLM.

